      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">(a + b + c)&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&ne; 0 and</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{a}{(3a\\space +\\space b\\space + \\space c)}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{b}{(a\\space +\\space 3b\\space + \\space c)}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{c}{(a\\space +\\space b\\space + \\space 3c)}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;= 3x</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">Calculation:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">(a + b + c)&nbsp;</span><span style=\"\">&ne; 0,</span></p>\n\n<p>So, we can assume the value of a, b and c</p>\n\n<p>Let the value of a = b = c = 1</p>\n\n<p>Now putting the value,&nbsp;<span style=\"\">a = b = c = 1 in that equation we get&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{a}{(3a\\space +\\space b\\space + \\space c)}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{b}{(a\\space +\\space 3b\\space + \\space c)}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp;</span><span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{c}{(a\\space +\\space b\\space + \\space 3c)}\\)</span><span style=\"\">&nbsp;=&nbsp; 1 / 5</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">So, 3x = 1 / 5</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; x = 1 / (3&nbsp;&times; 5)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 5</span><span style=\"\">x = 5 / 15</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr;&nbsp;</span>&nbsp;1 / 3</p>\n\n<p><strong>The value of 5x = 1 / 3</strong></p>\n",
